Public DICOMweb package selection
--------------------------------

Horos selects DicomWebClient and its DicomData dependency from the exact public
2.0.0-rc.1 package. The generated dictionary data preserves pertinent pydicom,
DCMTK, GDCM and dicom3tools notices. These notices do not imply that the package's
optional C++ codec runtimes, UI, server or ZIP products are linked by Horos.

The bundled original ThirdPartyNotices.txt and DistributionProvenance.json
describe the public package as a whole. They remain unmodified, including
credits for unselected products. The host's Package.resolved records its
effective resolution separately. swift-argument-parser 1.8.2 and ZIPFoundation
0.9.20 are resolved dependencies, without a product selected by the Horos target.
Downloads, full-package notices and source inventory do not establish runtime
incorporation. The release verifier checks the effective public checkout and
compares the selected notice bytes with that checkout before distribution.

VTK original source and installed binary adaptation
-------------------------------------------------

VTK 9.7.1 is acquired from its official release archive, with SHA-256
cae04fd355004cb916a409db79d53a208f1221e975aeacc7540ee67b148ee91a.
The source is read-only and has no source patches, including its FreeType and
MetaIO sources. The source record and original VTK copyright accompany the
compiled product in Resources/CompiledSources/VTK. Original FreeType, MetaIO
and other component license texts remain in Splash/ThirdParty/Native/VTK.

The host applies a Mach-O alias and symbol localization to the installed
FreeType module; it does not modify the original source. The separate
freetype-host-adaptation.json record identifies the source, configuration,
recipe, installed module and aggregate. It accompanies the source record in
Resources/CompiledSources/VTK. Binary adaptation does not replace the original
licenses or describe the resulting binaries as unmodified upstream artifacts.

Selected anonymization compatibility data
-----------------------------------------

HorosSelectedAnonymizationCatalog.h retains selected field metadata derived
from the GDCM 3.2.11 public dictionary. It preserves the original Mathieu
Malaterre/GDCM header; the full BSD copyright, conditions and disclaimer for
Mathieu Malaterre and CREATIS are reproduced without changes in
Binaries/Splash/ThirdParty/Compatibility/SelectedAnonymizationCatalog-Copyright.txt
and shipped with the application. This incorporated compatibility data is
listed separately from runtime libraries. The GDCM runtime library and build
target have been removed; the selected dictionary data remains incorporated.

